LocalFlow speech model
Its name in LocalFlow is kea-b-0.1. Renaming does not change the trained
weights, original model attribution, or CC-BY-4.0 license below.

kea-b-0.1

Model weights (the Core ML encoder, front-end constants, decoder and joint
weights and vocabulary in this directory): CC-BY-4.0, see LICENSE.
Software (the adapted native inference code in LocalFlow): MIT License, see
Software-LICENSE.

This model is a modified version of nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
(https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2, revision
ae9ad07059c7c739ffaf932226a8fe64ae2620b0), (c) NVIDIA, licensed CC-BY-4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The modified model is
distributed under the same license; see LICENSE. No endorsement by NVIDIA is
implied.

Changes made to the original model:
- It continues kea-b (https://huggingface.co/rajb3/kea-b), a binary
  derivative of the original. In kea-b, the feed-forward projections
  (feed_forward1/2.linear1/2), the self-attention projections (linear_q,
  linear_k, linear_v, linear_out, linear_pos) and the pointwise convolutions
  (conv.pointwise_conv1/2) of each of the 24 encoder layers were retrained
  with quantization-aware training as binary codes {-1, +1} with one scale
  per output row (264 matrices, 603,979,776 parameters), starting from the
  ternary model kea-t (https://huggingface.co/rajb3/kea-t).
- Those 264 binary matrices were trained for 97,137 more steps with
  quantization-aware training and 8-bit activations, distilling from a
  full-precision fine-tune of the original model on the labels below (not
  released). The prediction network and joint network were replaced by that
  fine-tune's and quantized to 8-bit integers with one scale per output
  channel, as was the subsampling output projection (pre_encode.out). The
  binary row scales are stored in FP16.
- For LocalFlow, the encoder was converted to a Core ML model holding only
  the 15-second input size: each binary matrix is stored as 1-bit codes with
  its FP16 row scale. The 8-bit weights are stored as the FP16 values the
  model computes with, and the prediction and joint networks are widened to
  FP32. The tokenizer and model configuration are unchanged from the
  original.

Training data (audio):
- YODAS-Granary, English
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/espnet/yodas-granary, revision
  969944574ea3f37890beaf67ea651e160cfaf043), CC-BY-3.0. References:
  "Yodas: Youtube-oriented dataset for audio and speech",
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.00899; "Granary: Speech Recognition and
  Translation Dataset in 25 European Languages",
  https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.13404.
- LibriSpeech train.clean.100, train.clean.360 and train.other.500
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/openslr/librispeech_asr, revision
  71cacbfb7e2354c4226d01e70d77d5fca3d04ba1), CC-BY-4.0.
- People's Speech, clean configuration
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/MLCommons/peoples_speech, revision
  f10597c5d3d3a63f8b6827701297c3afdf178272). The clean configuration selects
  CC-BY material; the CC-BY version (2.0, 2.5, 3.0 or 4.0) depends on the
  source recording.
- VoxPopuli, English train (https://huggingface.co/datasets/facebook/voxpopuli,
  revision 42f01879c780b4a2e90ec0b4f616c2ece526e4f1), CC0-1.0.
- AMI, IHM and SDM train (https://huggingface.co/datasets/edinburghcstr/ami,
  revision 46f28f2503e2ec48f8867a84eef356c70476beab), CC-BY-4.0; publisher
  license statement: https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/.
- Common Voice Scripted Speech 27.0, English
  (https://mozilladatacollective.com/datasets/cmu5jplf300nwmh07iqvk9leo,
  release 2026-09-17), CC0-1.0.
- Synthetic technical speech, generated with open-weight text-generation
  and speech-synthesis models whose licenses permit training use, with noise
  and reverberation augmentation.

Training targets were transcripts generated by
ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-2b
(https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-2b, revision
f4e68169fa2a5751acc4b5da9957855e5e8fc3f1), Apache-2.0, with punctuation from
the original model's transcripts, and cleaned by fixed rules and by
Qwen/Qwen3-8B (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B, revision
b968826d9c46dd6066d109eabc6255188de91218), Apache-2.0, choosing between
same-sound spellings. Common Voice clips use
their prompted sentences, and synthetic clips the sentences they were spoken
from.

